<article class="prose-page">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <%- include("../partials/college-notice.ejs") %>
    <p>These are the rules for using Dimora, written in plain language. By using the site you agree to them.</p>

    <h2>What this site is</h2>
    <p>Dimora is a college project. Bookings and payments are simulated, no real stay is arranged and no real money moves. Do not rely on the site for travel plans.</p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <p>Keep your password to yourself and give accurate details. You are responsible for what happens under your account.</p>

    <h2>What you post</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Only post listings, photos and reviews that are yours to share, and that are honest.</li>
        <li>No unlawful, hateful, harassing or misleading content, and no one else's personal information.</li>
        <li>You keep ownership of what you post. By posting it you let Dimora show it on the site.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Using the site fairly</h2>
    <p>Do not try to break the site, get into other people's accounts, or overload it with automated requests.</p>

    <h2>Removal and resets</h2>
    <p>We may remove content or accounts that break these rules. Because this is a project, data may also be reset or deleted at any time, and the site may be unavailable.</p>

    <h2>No guarantees</h2>
    <p>The site is provided as it is, without promises that it is accurate, always available or free of mistakes. To the extent the law allows, the people who built it are not liable for losses from using it.</p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>Ask on the <a href="https://github.com/lakshay-aggarwal-codes/Dimora/issues" rel="noopener noreferrer">project page</a>.</p>
</article>
